  "doc": {
    "title": "ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 v1.1 User Guide, section Header Block (tables J1 and J3)",
    "url": "https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-dev-kits/en/latest/esp32s3/esp32-s3-devkitc-1/user_guide_v1.1.html",
    "revision": "board ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 v1.1 (page 'latest' as retrieved)",
    "retrieved": "2026-11-26",
    "pinNumbering": "J1-n and J3-n are the header and the 'No.' column of the user guide's J1 and J3 tables (22 pins each, 44 total).",
    "notes": "GND is on J1-22, J3-1, J3-21 and J3-22 (labelled G in the tables; one board ground, group GND). 3V3 is on J1-1 and J1-2 (group 3V3, power_out from the on-board 5 V to 3.3 V LDO); 5V on J1-21 is power_in. GPIO pins are named GPIO<n> (with IO<n> and silkscreen number <n> as aliases), except J3-2 (TX, GPIO43) and J3-3 (RX, GPIO44). On v1.1 the on-board RGB LED is driven by GPIO38 (initial revision used GPIO48). No fixed interface roles: ESP32-S3 routes I2C and SPI through its GPIO matrix, so the user guide assigns none."
  },
